    "reason": "Issue 63 stage 2 (the Q6 ruling on #62, option C) moved the M1c identities from the whole installed source inventory to versioned semantic attestations declared in src/drift/domain/semantic_attestation.py: economic_validator_implementation_hash() in src/drift/markets/economic_validation.py now returns the m1c-source-validation-v1 attestation, and the selection, projection and composition stamps in src/drift/markets/economic_selection.py and src/drift/markets/economic_outcomes.py bind the m1c-evidence-v1 attestation. economic_implementation_hash() itself is unchanged and stays build and repository provenance only. That edit changed the bytes of the three paths listed in superseded_paths, so the v2 pin for each no longer describes the live working tree. v2 still describes commit aecee94 exactly, stays preserved, and still authenticates the aecee94 archive that replays the M1c history; it is superseded only as the working-tree source freeze. semantic_attestation.py postdates this freeze and is pinned by the M1d chain (m1d-v7), not here. No historical fixture or archive pin changes: pinned replay still recomputes each M1c generation's original identity from its own archived source."
  },
